  "body": "Possibly as two different endpoints. Users should be able to leave - this is just for an admin bootstrapping groups.\r\n\r\nThis is for FOSDEM.\r\n\r\nProposed endpoints (for server admins, **not** group admins):\r\n* `POST /_synapse/admin/v1/groups/+group:example.org/join/@user:example.org` (empty request body)\r\n  * Only works for force-joining local users to local groups. Fails with error otherwise.\r\n  * If the group is invite only then the group admin implicitly invites the user before doing the join.\r\n* `POST /_synapse/admin/v1/users/@user:example.org/groups/+group:example.org/update_publicity` (request body of `{\"publicise\":true}` to match self-serve group API)\r\n  * Also only works for local users, though remote groups should be possible given this sort of setting doesn't touch the actual group object. Fails with error otherwise.\r\n\r\nPossible alternatives:\r\n* An appservice which has full control over the entire user space and can then impersonate each user on its own.\r\n  * Not great because users might briefly still receive an invite to the group while the appservice does the second request, which might fail. This could result in a momentary bing noise.\r\n\r\n",
